# The search-index module's own texts: its name and the line under it, the
# hint of its mark, its page — where the index stands and what it reads — and
# the questions and refusals of what is changed there.
brain-task-search-index = Keep the search index
brain-task-search-index-does = Starts fast-access's index of your files, what they say, the manual pages, the programs you can install and your videos, when it is not running — waiting for a quiet machine, since its first walk of a home is minutes of disk. While it builds the index from scratch, a mark on the modeline says so; afterwards it follows your changes as they happen.
search-index-why-when-stopped = When it is not running
search-index-why-not-a-folder = That is not a folder that exists, written from the root (/home/…).
search-index-why-not-a-skip = Leave out a name (build) or a whole path (/home/…/videos), not part of one.
search-index-why-unkept = What it reads (index.json) could not be written, or does not parse and was left as it is.
search-index-mark-building = The search index is being built from the start
search-index-heading-now = The index now
search-index-heading-reads = What it reads
search-index-state = State
search-index-state-walking = Walking your folders
search-index-state-following = Following your changes
search-index-state-stopped = Not running
search-index-documents = Documents
search-index-size = On disk
search-index-committed = Last written
search-index-never = Not yet
search-index-root = Folder
search-index-home = Your home folder
search-index-add-root = Add a folder…
search-index-contents = What files say
search-index-hidden = Hidden files
search-index-on = read
search-index-off = not read
search-index-skip = Left out
search-index-add-skip = Leave something out…
search-index-unreadable = What it reads (index.json) does not parse; the index keeps what it had.
cmd-search-index-add-root = Index another folder
cmd-search-index-forget-root = Stop indexing this folder
cmd-search-index-contents = Read what files say, or only their names
cmd-search-index-hidden = Index hidden files too, or not
cmd-search-index-add-skip = Leave a name or a path out of the index
cmd-search-index-forget-skip = Index this again
ask-search-index-add-root = Folder to index
ask-search-index-add-skip = Name or path to leave out
